ocessed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number only is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast with a localizing needle and accompanying specimen X ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white stellate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm lesion extending to within 0 5cm of the closest inked margin  A representative section is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Sections of mass are submitted in cassettes A B  Representative sections of breast  submitted in cassettes C E  A portion of the lesion is taken by Dr  Deutch  Received in two container  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm aggregate mass of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes F through Q  Labeled  additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE unoriented piece of breast tissue  Sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes R through T  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART C  ROGHT BREAST  ADDITIONAL MARGIN   report_end  , Positive.
