this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass  is a 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch on one of the bulbous ends  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal two yellow firm nodules measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm in average size and focal gritty areas  one present around stitched tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Stitch area submitted in A and B  remainder submitted in C through J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass   2  is a 3 x 2 x 0 4cm mass of fibrofatty tissue  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue  fat  and a subtle faint nodularity  No frozen done  Specimen submitted entirely in K through N  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS AREAS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS AREAS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Eug